-#
  A terminal failure: the install could not be started and there is nothing in the form for the
  user to correct (the backend was unreachable, or the daemon refused the request). So this
  drops the fields and keeps only the reason.

  A validation failure does NOT use this partial -- it re-renders `new` with the form intact,
  because there the user's next move is to fix the input. See AppInstallsController#render_form.

= turbo_stream.update("modal-frame") do
  = v.modal(t("app_installs.title"), size: "md", close_button: false) do |modal|
    = v.alert("danger", icon: "x-circle") do
      .mb-2.fw-bold= t("app_installs.failed")
      %div= @error
